NOTE
Tutorial 2 — Creating a Quorum Slice.
Planning timestamps generated from the script's scene budgets.
Re-time against the final edit before publishing (see docs/video-tutorials.md).

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.400
A quorum slice is your personal trust
network.

2
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:14.400
It lists the institutions you trust to
vouch for you, such as your university,

3
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:21.400
your licensing body, and a former
employer.

4
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:28.400
Each attestor has a weight from one to one
hundred, and the slice has a

5
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.539
threshold.

6
00:00:30.639 --> 00:00:37.539
A credential is trusted once the combined
weight of attestors who signed it

7
00:00:37.639 --> 00:00:42.458
reaches that threshold.

8
00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:22.400
For this demo we'll create four testnet
identities: the holder, a university, an

9
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:29.400
engineering society, and an employer.

10
00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:36.400
Export the quorum_proof contract ID from
the previous video so we can reuse it.

11
00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:22.400
Now call create_slice.

12
00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:29.400
The holder is the creator and signs the
transaction.

13
00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:36.400
We pass three attestors with weights
forty, forty, and twenty, and a threshold

14
00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:39.616
of sixty.

15
00:02:39.716 --> 00:02:46.616
That means any two of the university and
society, or either one plus the

16
00:02:46.716 --> 00:02:53.616
employer, is enough.

17
00:02:53.716 --> 00:03:00.616
The contract returns the new slice ID.

18
00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:07.400
Let's read it back, first directly from
the contract with get_slice, then

19
00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:14.400
through the REST API.

20
00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:21.400
Both show the same attestors, weights, and
threshold.

21
00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:28.400
Verifiers will usually use the API.

22
00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:22.400
You created a weighted quorum slice and
read it back two ways.

23
00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:29.400
Choose weights carefully; no single
attestor should be able to reach the

24
00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:36.400
threshold alone unless you intend that.

25
00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:43.400
Next, we'll issue a credential and have
the slice attest to it.
